# gitleaks allow-list. Add fingerprints reported by `gitleaks detect` that
# are confirmed safe (e.g. test fixtures, public API keys, documentation
# placeholders). Format: <commit-sha>:<file-path>:<rule-id>:<line-number>
#
# Each entry MUST be paired with a code comment in the offending file
# explaining why the match is innocuous. If you can't justify a code
# comment, you can't justify the allow-list entry.
#
# This file starts empty. CI's `secrets` job will fail if anything new
# trips — review the finding, rotate if real, allow-list (with comment)
# if not.
